  "slides": [
    {
      "page_title": "Cheat Sheet And Mental Model",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "One Question Decides Everything"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Is the change unstaged, staged, committed-local, or pushed?",
            "That one answer picks the command — nothing else matters"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "State",
            "Undo"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Unstaged",
              "`git restore`"
            ],
            [
              "Staged",
              "`restore --staged`"
            ],
            [
              "Committed local",
              "`git reset`"
            ],
            [
              "Pushed",
              "`git revert`"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Reset Depth Ladder"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Mode",
            "Rewinds"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "`--soft`",
              "HEAD"
            ],
            [
              "`--mixed`",
              "HEAD + Index"
            ],
            [
              "`--hard`",
              "HEAD + Index + Working"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Safety Ranking"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Safest: `revert`, then `restore --staged`",
            "Then `reset --soft`, then `reset --mixed`",
            "Then `restore`, then `reset --hard`",
            "Most destructive: `git clean -fdx`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Worked Example: Reset Too Far"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git reset --hard HEAD~3  # oops, too far",
            "git reflog              # find the old tip",
            "git reset --hard HEAD@{1}  # back in place"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Rewrite Or Append?",
          "text": "Did anyone else pull it? Yes → revert, which appends history. No → reset, which rewrites it. `commit --amend` replaces the tip commit only, and after a push it needs `git push --force-with-lease`, never bare `--force`."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Three Things To Trust"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Cheat Sheet And Mental Model (cont.)",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Reflog undoes anything that moved a ref",
            "No reflog exists for working-tree content",
            "`ORIG_HEAD` = one-step undo from reset, merge, rebase, pull",
            "Stash is commits in disguise — fsck finds it after a drop"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Stash In One Breath"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`git stash push -m \"wip auth\"` labels the entry",
            "`-u` includes untracked, `-a` adds ignored too",
            "`pop` = apply + drop; `apply` keeps the entry"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Recovery Window"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "headers": [
            "Thing",
            "Survives"
          ],
          "rows": [
            [
              "Unreachable, via reflog",
              "~30 days"
            ],
            [
              "Prune grace period",
              "2 weeks"
            ],
            [
              "After `git gc` runs",
              "gone"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Cheap Insurance"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "bash",
          "lines": [
            "git branch backup-$(date +%s)  # snapshot",
            "git stash -u  # park everything, untracked too"
          ],
          "runnable": false
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Commit early and often on a local branch",
            "A commit makes every later mistake reversible"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "takeaway",
          "title": "The One True Limit",
          "text": "Everything Git tracks is recoverable except working-tree changes that were never added and never committed. That is the only point of no return."
        }
      ],
      "cont": true
    }
  ],
  "caption": {
    "text": "Part 2 of GIT UNDO: THE FIELD MANUAL. \"I lost my commits with reset --hard\" is almost always false — the commits are still sitting in your reflog. This field manual walks every undo Git gives you: the three trees underneath them all, reset's three depths, revert for anything already pushed, restore, stash, and fsck rescues for work you thought was gone. Save it for the day your stomach drops.",
